# Commit-reset state machines

Do not walk a multi-stage UI flow with nested event `if`s and a copied reset on every return. Put the walk position in a small state type whose commit/cancel path always clears it. Put the option tree, payload shape, and post-commit side effects in a catalog/table.

```cpp
// BAD — reset duplicated on every exit; new events must touch every branch
if (stage_ == First && event_ == "PS") {
  emit tagCommitted(...);
  clearUi(); event_.clear(); first_.clear(); stage_ = None;
  return;
}

// GOOD — one advance, one commit; takeCommit() resets
followUpState_.select(choice);
if (FollowUpCatalog::optionsAfter(followUpState_.mainEvent(),
                                  followUpState_.selections()).isEmpty()) {
  const auto snapshot = followUpState_.takeCommit();
  emit tagCommitted(snapshot.mainEvent, FollowUpCatalog::formatPayload(...));
  clearUi();
}
```

Adding a follow-up event means extending `FollowUpCatalog`, not `onFollowUpButtonClicked()`.
